From: postmarketOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] scripts/dtc: share the parser location object

Modern toolchains use -fno-common by default.  This old downstream kernel
defines yylloc in both generated DTC objects, causing the host dtc build to
fail before the ARM64 kernel is compiled.  The parser owns the object; make
the lexer reference it instead.

--- a/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.lex.c_shipped
+++ b/scripts/dtc/dtc-lexer.lex.c_shipped
@@ -637,7 +637,7 @@ char *yytext;
 #include "srcpos.h"
 #include "dtc-parser.tab.h"
 
-YYLTYPE yylloc;
+extern YYLTYPE yylloc;
 extern bool treesource_error;
 
 /* CAUTION: this will stop working if we ever use yyless() or yyunput() */
